.TH SRS-ROOT 1 "October 2026" "srs-sysinfo 2.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
srs-root \- collect root-only hardware data for srs-gui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec srs-root
.br
.B srs-root \-\-user
.I NAME
.br
.B pkexec srs-root \-\-acpi\-eval
.I METHOD
.RI [ ARG ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects data that only root can read and hands it to the invoking user in
.IR ~/.cache/srs/root/ :
dmidecode, decode-dimms (DIMM SPD), smartctl and nvme SMART logs, MSR reads,
full PCI configuration space and copies of the ACPI tables.
Since 2.4 also, where they apply:
.I umc.txt
(AMD Ryzen 7000 / 9000 desktop memory controller registers, read through the ryzen_smu driver's
.I smn
file: the 4-byte address written there only selects what is read, the 8-byte form that writes is never used;
each value is read twice under
.IR /run/lock/srs-smn.lock ),
.I intel-imc.txt
(Intel Core 6th gen to Core Ultra memory timings, experimental: the MCHBAR window mapped read-only, aligned 32-bit reads, never switched on),
.I aod.bin
and
.I aod.txt
(the BIOS's AMD AOD memory settings table, from /dev/mem only when the kernel allows it, i.e. iomem=relaxed on kernels with IO_STRICT_DEVMEM),
.I rapl.txt
(AMD energy counters read twice, one second apart),
.I ebda.txt
and
.I ebda.bin
(the EBDA pointer at 0x40E and, if present, the EBDA below 0xA0000),
.I vbios\-<pci>.bin
(each AMD GPU driver's own VBIOS copy from debugfs; the GPU's ROM is not touched),
.I gpio.txt
(the kernel's debugfs GPIO table),
.I efi\-systab.txt
and
.I esrt.txt
(UEFI System Table pointers and ESRT entries).
Two opt-ins, set in srs-gui's Options and read from
.IR ~/.config/srs/SRSDEF.ini :
.B Read DIMM PMIC=1
writes
.I pmic\-*.txt
(each DDR5 PMIC's registers 0x00\-0x3F with
.BR "i2cdump \-y \-r 0x00\-0x3F" ,
byte reads, no \-f), and
.B Read EC=1
writes
.I ec.bin
(the embedded controller's 256 registers through ec_sys loaded with write_support=0, unloaded again if srs-root loaded it).
When collecting it only reads from the hardware; nothing is written to devices
(see \-\-acpi\-eval for the one exception, which you start).
USB-attached disks are skipped for SMART unless
.B SRS_SMART_USB=1
is set.
.PP
.B srs-gui
runs it through
.BR pkexec (1)
(one password prompt). The template unit
.B srs-root@.service
runs it once per boot for one user, as
.BR "srs-root \-\-user " NAME ;
srs-gui enables it from Menu \(-> Options \(-> Refresh root data at boot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
collect for user NAME (root only; used by srs-root@NAME.service).
.TP
.BI \-\-acpi\-eval " METHOD " "[ARG...]"
(2.4) evaluate one ACPI method through the acpi_call kernel module and exit; nothing else is collected.
srs-gui's Tools \(-> ACPI method evaluation runs this, after a one-time warning.
METHOD must be an ACPI name path such as \e_SB.PCI0.GPP0._STA; each ARG a number (decimal or 0x hex),
a "string" (letters, digits, space, . _ \-) or a buffer b followed by hex bytes; at most 7.
Anything else exits 2 without running; exit 3 when acpi_call is not installed.
The result is printed and logged with the time to
.IR ~/.cache/srs/root/acpi\-calls.txt .
.B This runs BIOS code and can change hardware state
(switch devices, fan, power or performance settings, BIOS settings, or hang or reboot the PC).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR srs-gui (1)
